sn35.247:4.6 | S: And they truly understand the freedom of heart and freedom by wisdom where those arisen bad, unskillful qualities cease without remainder. | T: He discerns, as it has come to be, the awareness-release, the discernment-release, where all evil, unskillful mental qualities that have arisen utterly cease without remainder.
sn35.247:5.1 | S: Suppose a person was to catch six animals, with diverse territories and feeding grounds, and tie them up with a strong rope. | T: “Just as if a person, catching six animals of different ranges, of different habitats, were to bind them with a strong rope.
sn35.247:5.2 | S: They’d catch a snake, | T: Catching a snake, he would bind it with a strong rope.
sn35.247:5.3 | S: a dolphin, | T: Catching a crocodile…
