## sn35.24
sn35.24:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, I will teach you the principle for giving up the all. | T: “Monks, I will teach you the All as a phenomenon to be abandoned.
sn35.24:1.2 | S: Listen … | T: Listen & pay close attention. I will speak.”
sn35.24:1.3 | S: And what is the principle for giving up the all? | T: “As you say, lord,” the monks responded to him. The Blessed One said, “And which All is a phenomenon to be abandoned?
sn35.24:1.4 | S: The eye should be given up. Sights should be given up. Eye consciousness should be given up. Eye contact should be given up. The painful, pleasant, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on eye contact should also be given up. | T: The eye is to be abandoned. Forms are to be abandoned. Eye-consciousness is to be abandoned. Eye-contact is to be abandoned. And whatever there is that arises in dependence on eye-contact—experienced as pleasure, pain or neither-pleasure-nor-pain—that too is to be abandoned.
sn35.24:1.5 | S: The ear … nose … | T: “The ear is to be abandoned. Sounds are to be abandoned… “The nose is to be abandoned. Aromas are to be abandoned…
sn35.24:1.6 | S: tongue … | T: “The tongue is to be abandoned. Flavors are to be abandoned…
sn35.24:1.7 | S: body … | T: “The body is to be abandoned. Tactile sensations are to be abandoned…
sn35.24:1.8 | S: mind should be given up. Ideas should be given up. Mind consciousness should be given up. Mind contact should be given up. The painful, pleasant, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on mind contact should be given up. | T: “The intellect is to be abandoned. Ideas are to be abandoned. Intellect-consciousness is to be abandoned. Intellect-contact is to be abandoned. And whatever there is that arises in dependence on intellect-contact—experienced as pleasure, pain or neither-pleasure-nor-pain—that too is to be abandoned.
sn35.24:1.9 | S: This is the principle for giving up the all.” | T: “This is called the All as a phenomenon to be abandoned.”
sn35.24:1.10 | P: Dutiyaṁ. | T: (none)


